===Recurring Schedule===
The <code>Recurring Schedule</code> part will only have to be updated if blitz events are added to this template or if a new regular event is released. Each entry contains a set of data about an event. The first item is the full event name, and the second item is a value telling how the schedule is defined for the event (week, year, month). The third item is a date value describing when the event starts. Its meaning changes for each schedule type (MONTH:DD:HH:MM for year, WEEKDAYNUM:HH:MM for week, DD:HH:MM for month). The fourth item is another date value describing the length of the event in days, hours, and minutes in the same format. The date format is identical for all schedule types (DD:HH:MM). Note that all events put on here will automatically be shown in the Recurring Events tab of this template.

Some events are purposely not included in this data page that have obvious schedules. These include the Weekday Stages (Monday Stage, Tuesday Stage, etc.) and the Growing Stages (Growing Green, Growing Purple, etc.). A more complete data page is found at [[Template:EventClock/recurring.json]].

===Images===
When a new uber is added to a set or a gacha banner is otherwise updated, the banner images for the set should be updated to the newest available ones. While it is better to keep this updated, it is not a major issue if this is outdated. However, if a gacha banner image is missing from this module, it must be added. New additions should be in the following format: <code>"[full set name]": "<a href='/wiki/[page name with spaces replaced by underscores]'><img src='[image url]' title='[Event Name]' width='300px'></a>",</code>. Note that for each regular gacha set, there are three images included for each of them: the lowest ID banner image, the Neneko and Friends version, and the Reinforcements version.

If an image for an event is missing (indicated by a broken image in this template), it should be added after finding an appropriate image in the format: <code>"<Full Event Name>": "<image in html>",</code>. Arguments such as the image size should be adjusted to look good for each image. For collaboration event images, the size is 300px, and map names have a size of 192px.

